    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4267A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto authorize the county of Schuyler to convey to Seneca\nHarbor Place, LLC, an easement through land located in the county's\nSeneca Harbor Park\n\nPURPOSE:\nAuthorizes Schuyler County to convey an easement through land\nlocated in Seneca Harbor Park to enable access to lake front\ndevelopment\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1. The county of Schuyler, acting by\nand through its county legislature, is hereby authorized to convey by\nappropriate instruments to Dorothy and Henry F. Lembeck IV, an\neasement located in Seneca Harbor Park and described in section three\nof this act, for the purpose of enabling access to lakefront\ndevelopment.\n\nSection 2. The authorization provided in section one of this act shall\nbe effective only upon the condition that the county of Schuyler\nacquire and dedicate as parkland the lands described in section four\nof this act. In the event that the land to be dedicated is less in\nfair market value to the easement being granted, the county shall\ndedicate the difference to either the acquisition of new parklands\nand/or capital improvements to existing park and recreational\nfacilities.\n\nSection 3. The easement to be conveyed by the county of Schuyler\npursuant to section one of this act is described as follows: ALL THAT\nTRACT OR PARCEL OF LAND situate in the Village of Watkins Glen,\nCounty of Schuyler and State of New York.\n\nSection 4. The land to be dedicated as parkland pursuant to section\ntwo of this act is described as follows: ALL that tract or parcel of\nland situate in Town of Dix, County of Schuyler and State of New York\nbeing more particularly bounded and described as follows: Beginning\nat a Point located along the Southerly shore of Seneca Lake, said\npoint being a North-easterly comer of lands now or formerly of the\nCounty of Schuyler (Liber 377 of Deeds, page 298), and a\nNorth-westerly comer of lands now or formerly of the Village of\nWatkins Glen (Liber 306 Deeds, page 543); Thence\n\nSection 6. This act shall take effect immediately.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nA 2008 study identified a critical housing shortage in\nSchuyler County. Allowing Schuyler County to grant a permanent\neasement at Seneca Harbor Park would allow access to lake front\n\ndevelopment of adjoining property and creation of a major economic\nasset for the entire county. The portion of the park in question is\ncurrently utilized as a parking/driveway area and such use will not\nchange as a result of this action. The aforementioned development is\ncontingent on Seneca Harbor Place, LLC obtaining access to their\nproperty through this portion of the park.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n2010 - S.8134A, A.11412A\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
